le('button').not(':disabled, [aria-disabled=\"true\"]')\n\nThe cy.getByRole() API reference covers every option, including shadow DOM, TypeScript, and scoping with .within().\n\nWhy native elements are the default in cy.getByRole()\n\nFor any role that HTML has a native element for, such as button, link, heading, dialog, or checkbox, cy.getByRole() matches only elements whose tag gives them that role. A <div role=\"button\"> does not match cy.getByRole('button') unless you pass native: false.\n\n<button>Save</button>\n<div role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\">Cancel</div>\n// Yields and clicks the nati …[truncated]","reasoning":"The text contains a substantial, coherent article body about Cypress's cy.getByRole() with multiple sections, code examples, and explanatory paragraphs. Despite being truncated, it clearly represents a real, meaningful article.","titlePath":["Content quality @upstream","Live Feed: every probed card renders a real article in the reader"],"testFile":"tests/contentQuality.spec.ts","retry":0,"timestamp":"2026-10-17T11:46:03.285Z"}
